A||||7||BOILERMAKER||Dogbone Differences
Z||000000||BOILERMAKER||05-12-99||07:12 AM||||I know there are differences between dogbones of the 6cyl and the 4cyl of the Fiero, but is there a difference (in length) between different years of the V6?  <p>I recently changed a shot dogbone and noticed a different dogbone was put in (actually I took parts off of a different 6 and switched mine out).  Anyway, I was wondering if there were different lengths for different years.<p>What difference would I see in the driving characteristics of the car if a different length was put in???<p>Thanks
Z||000001||theogre||05-12-99||11:43 AM||||the lenght won't matter much as long as they are in the same location. the stiffness of the bushings matters most.
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||05-15-99||12:08 AM||||All V6s have the same dog bone. If the dog bone is black and made of round tuning it could be an after market unit as sold by the Fiero Store.
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||05-15-99||12:09 AM||||oops.....tubing not tuning....:)
Z||000004||BOILERMAKER||05-17-99||07:07 AM||||Well, thanks for the information.  I beg to differ as far as all of the dogbones being the same.  The one I took off was a V6 Fiero dogbone and was a different length (not significant as seen between the 4 and 6 dogbones) and the other dogbone was taken off of a GT.<p>None of these were black.  Unless the previous owners changed them out (nothing is impossible), I haven't seen an aftermarket item such as this on either fiero.
Z||000005||Carrolles||05-17-99||04:59 PM||||I believe all of the v-6s have the same length dog bone but the 85 (and I believe the 86) have a cylindrical insert bushing while the 87 and 88 have tapered bushings.  You would have to know this if you were to order replacement bushings.<br>Hope this helps,<br>Carroll
Z||000006||SCCA FIERO||05-17-99||07:08 PM||||Hmm... Well ALL V6 fieros use the same length dogbone. Maybe somebody put the wrong one in somehow. The cavaliers had a dogbone similar to the fiero.....Hard to tell.
Z||000007||theogre||05-17-99||07:22 PM||||like I said.... the length really doesn't matter. as long as the "new" one isn't pulling the engine over so far things are hitting stuff. A 1/2-1 inch +- isn't going to matter.
